---
import EngineDiagram from './EngineDiagram.astro';
interface Props {
  kind: 'engine' | 'definitions' | 'composition' | 'versions';
}
const { kind } = Astro.props;
---

{kind === 'engine' && <EngineDiagram />}

{kind === 'definitions' && (
  <figure class="diagram definitions" aria-label="Shop source tables become named metrics and dimensions">
    <div class="source-chain">
      <div class="source"><strong>Stores</strong><span>One row per store</span></div>
      <span class="chain-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="source"><strong>Orders</strong><span>One row per purchase</span></div>
      <span class="chain-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="source"><strong>Order lines</strong><span>One row per receipt line</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="connection-label">One store has many orders. One order has many lines.</p>
    <div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <div class="definition-model">
      <div class="node-heading"><span class="diagram-kicker">Your semantic model</span><strong>The shop’s reporting rules</strong></div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Revenue</dt><dd>Sum each order’s subtotal, excluding tax.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Order count</dt><dd>Count purchases, even when they have several lines.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Line count</dt><dd>Count receipt lines independently of order measures.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Store name</dt><dd>Group orders and their lines by the same store.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <div class="result-node">Aggregate orders and lines separately, then combine by store.</div>
    <figcaption>The model declares each dataset’s grain and relationships. Queries select metrics and supported grouping dimensions.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{kind === 'composition' && (
  <figure class="diagram composition" aria-label="Two models aggregate independently and join on a declared shared region dimension">
    <div class="branches">
      <div class="branch"><span class="diagram-kicker">Sales model</span><strong>Revenue</strong><span>Its own source rows<br />Its own approved definition</span><div class="branch-output">One result per region</div></div>
      <div class="branch"><span class="diagram-kicker">Planning model</span><strong>Budget</strong><span>Its own source rows<br />Its own approved definition</span><div class="branch-output">One result per region</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="merge-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
    <div class="join-node"><strong>Join on the declared shared dimension</strong><span>Same region meaning · compatible types · complete keys</span></div>
    <div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <div class="result-columns"><span>region</span><span>revenue</span><span>budget</span></div>
    <figcaption>Crossfield aggregates each model first, then joins the results. Matching column names alone do not authorize a join.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

{kind === 'versions' && (
  <figure class="diagram versions" aria-label="Two Jaffle model revisions calculate different revenue definitions over the same source rows">
    <div class="result-node"><strong>The same shop data</strong><span>525 orders · the same source rows</span></div>
    <div class="merge-lines split-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
    <div class="branches">
      <div class="branch"><span class="diagram-kicker">Revision 1 · jaffle_old</span><strong>Revenue includes tax</strong><span>Sum of order totals</span><div class="version-amount">$6,730.75</div></div>
      <div class="branch current"><span class="diagram-kicker">Revision 2 · jaffle_current</span><strong>Revenue excludes tax</strong><span>Sum of order subtotals</span><div class="version-amount">$6,355.00</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="merge-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
    <div class="result-node"><strong>Current − previous: <span class="amount">−$375.75</span></strong><span>The difference is the collected tax.</span></div>
    <figcaption>Precomputed results from the frozen shop example. Model revisions preserve definitions; the underlying source data remains live.</figcaption>
  </figure>
)}

<style>
  .diagram { margin: 0; min-width: 0; color: var(--color-soil-900); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .diagram strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .diagram :is(.source, .branch, .result-node, .join-node) > span:not(.diagram-kicker) { display: block; margin-top: .4rem; color: var(--color-soil-700); font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .diagram figcaption { margin-top: 1.1rem; color: var(--color-soil-700); font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .connector { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .6rem; min-height: 2.5rem; color: var(--color-field-700); font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .result-node { padding: .85rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); background: var(--color-soil-100); border-radius: .45rem; text-align: center; font-size: .875rem; }
  .source-chain { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.25rem 1fr 1.25rem 1fr; align-items: center; gap: .25rem; }
  .source { padding: .9rem .5rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); text-align: center; font-size: .8125rem; }
  .source > span { font-size: .6875rem !important; }
  .chain-arrow { text-align: center; color: var(--color-soil-700); }
  .connection-label { margin-top: .65rem; color: var(--color-soil-700); text-align: center; font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .definition-model { border: 1px solid var(--color-field-700); border-radius: .65rem; background: #fffdf7; overflow: hidden; }
  .node-heading { padding: 1rem 1.2rem; background: #f0f3e9; }
  .diagram-kicker { display: block; color: var(--color-sun-700); font-size: .6875rem; letter-spacing: .04em; margin-bottom: .4rem; }
  .node-heading strong { display: block; font-size: 1rem; }
  .definition-model dl { margin: 0; padding: 0 1.2rem; }
  .definition-model dl > div { padding: .85rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-soil-200); }
  .definition-model dl > div:last-child { border: 0; }
  .definition-model dt { font-size: .8125rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .definition-model dd { margin: .25rem 0 0; color: var(--color-soil-700); font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .branches { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .branch { min-width: 0; padding: 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); border-radius: .6rem; background: #fffdf7; }
  .branch > strong { display: block; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .branch-output { margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: .75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); color: var(--color-field-700); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .merge-lines { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); height: 2rem; margin-inline: 25%; }
  .merge-lines span { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .merge-lines span:first-child { border-left: 1px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .merge-lines span:last-child { border-right: 1px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .join-node { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-field-700); border-radius: .5rem; background: #f0f3e9; text-align: center; font-size: .875rem; }
  .result-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); border: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); background: var(--color-soil-100); }
  .result-columns span { padding: .8rem .35rem; text-align: center; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .75rem; border-right: 1px solid var(--color-soil-300); }
  .result-columns span:last-child { border: 0; }
  .split-lines { transform: rotate(180deg); }
  .current { border-color: var(--color-field-700); background: #f0f3e9; }
  .version-amount { margin-top: 1rem; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: clamp(1.15rem,2.5vw,1.8rem); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 500; }
  .amount { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  @media(max-width:450px) { .branch { padding: .85rem .65rem; } .branch > strong { font-size: .875rem; } .branches { gap: .65rem; } }
</style>
